WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.126
One mild October evening, Anne leaned back in her chair and sighed.

2
00:00:17.127 --> 00:00:22.223
She was sitting at a table covered with textbooks and exercises.

3
00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:25.638
"What is the matter?" asked Gilbert, who had just arrived.

4
00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:31.752
"How's school going? I heard you are doing a splendid job and all the children like you."

5
00:00:31.753 --> 00:00:40.199
"Actually, no, not all," said Anne. "Anthony Pye doesn't and won't like me.

6
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.805
And what's worse is he doesn't respect me.

7
00:00:42.806 --> 00:00:46.581
I don't mind confessing to you that it worries me miserably.

8
00:00:46.582 --> 00:00:52.180
I've tried every way to win him over, and I'm beginning to fear I never shall.

9
00:00:52.181 --> 00:00:56.264
But we'll see what patience and kindness can do."

10
00:00:56.265 --> 00:01:01.954
"Do you at least like teaching?" asked Gilbert. "I do.

11
00:01:01.955 --> 00:01:07.751
Why, I've learned more in the past few weeks of teaching than in all the years I went to school myself!"

12
00:01:07.752 --> 00:01:14.789
Anne and Gilbert talked for a while about their plans, and Gilbert announced that he wanted to study to be a doctor.

13
00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:20.165
"I want to do my share of honest, real work in the world, Anne."

14
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:25.580
"I'd like to add some beauty to life," said Anne dreamily.

15
00:01:25.581 --> 00:01:32.097
"I don't exactly want to make people know more—though I know that teaching is the noblest ambition—

16
00:01:32.098 --> 00:01:38.338
but I'd love for people to have some little joy or happy thought because of me."

17
00:01:38.339 --> 00:01:44.277
"I think you're fulfilling that ambition every day," said Gilbert admiringly.

18
00:01:44.278 --> 00:01:50.845
Gilbert left, and when Marilla returned home, the fire was crackling and Anne had dinner ready.

19
00:01:50.846 --> 00:01:54.470
But Marilla sank wearily into her chair.

20
00:01:54.471 --> 00:01:59.890
"Are your eyes troubling you? Does your head ache?" queried Anne anxiously.

21
00:01:59.891 --> 00:02:06.971
"No," said Marilla. "I'm just tired . . . and worried about my cousin Mary and her children.

22
00:02:06.972 --> 00:02:10.970
Mary is very ill and may die soon."

23
00:02:10.971 --> 00:02:15.702
"What are the children like? How old are they?" Anne asked.

24
00:02:15.703 --> 00:02:20.607
"They're twins—six years old," replied Marilla.

25
00:02:20.608 --> 00:02:29.781
"Oh, I've always been especially interested in twins since Mrs. Hammond had so many," said Anne eagerly. "Are they pretty?"

26
00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:35.221
"Goodness, I couldn't tell," said Marilla. "They were too dirty.

27
00:02:35.222 --> 00:02:40.685
Davy was making mud pies outside, and he pushed Dora into the mud.

28
00:02:40.686 --> 00:02:49.369
Mary said Dora was really a very good child but that Davy was full of mischief." Marilla paused for a moment.

29
00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.128
"Anne, I'm sure Mary wants me to take those children.

30
00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:57.412
She didn't say so, but I'm sure she thinks it."

31
00:02:57.413 --> 00:03:01.683
"Oh!" Anne clasped her hands with excitement.

32
00:03:01.684 --> 00:03:05.133
"And of course you will, Marilla, won't you?"

33
00:03:05.134 --> 00:03:09.194
"I haven't made up my mind," said Marilla.

34
00:03:09.195 --> 00:03:17.070
Marilla thought there was only one thing you could say about twins: they were twice as bad as a single child.

35
00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:23.918
"I think twins are very interesting," repeated Anne. "At least one pair of them."

36
00:03:23.919 --> 00:03:30.543
Marilla frowned and said, "Dora seems good and quiet, but that Davy . . ."

37
00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:39.014
Anne was fond of children, and the memory of her own lonely childhood before she came to Green Gables was still very vivid.

38
00:03:39.015 --> 00:03:43.810
"It's our duty to look after them, Marilla," Anne insisted.

39
00:03:43.811 --> 00:03:48.716
"I suppose it is," Marilla agreed with some reluctance.

40
00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:53.143
"Don't look so happy, Anne. It will mean extra work for you.

41
00:03:53.144 --> 00:04:00.534
My eyes are bad, so you'll have to make their clothes. And you don't like sewing."

42
00:04:00.535 --> 00:04:08.923
"I do hate sewing," said Anne calmly, "but it's good for people to do things they don't like . . . in moderation."

43
00:04:08.924 --> 00:04:14.012
A few weeks later, Mrs. Lynde was sitting at her kitchen window, knitting.

44
00:04:14.013 --> 00:04:18.238
Five years previously, Mrs. Lynde had sat at the same window

45
00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:25.199
and watched Matthew Cuthbert drive past with Anne when the young girl first arrived in Avonlea.

46
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:34.201
"There's Marilla coming home from her cousin's funeral," Mrs. Lynde said to her husband, "and she's got the twins with her.

47
00:04:34.202 --> 00:04:43.952
Yes, there's Davy trying to grab the pony's tail and Marilla jerking him back. Dora's sitting up straight.

48
00:04:43.953 --> 00:04:48.204
She always looks as if she's just been starched and ironed."

49
00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:56.739
The pony jogged past the Lyndes' farm and along the lane to Green Gables. Marilla's face was rather grim.

50
00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:03.048
She could not make Davy sit still and worried that he might fall off the buggy and break his neck.

51
00:05:03.049 --> 00:05:06.821
In despair she finally threatened to smack him.

52
00:05:06.822 --> 00:05:14.741
Whereupon Davy climbed into her lap, flung his chubby arms about her neck, and gave her a bear-like hug.

53
00:05:14.742 --> 00:05:20.978
"I don't believe you mean it," Davy said, touching her wrinkled cheek affectionately.

54
00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:24.345
"You don't look like a lady who'd smack a little boy.

55
00:05:24.346 --> 00:05:28.050
Didn't you find it hard to keep still when you were little?"

56
00:05:28.051 --> 00:05:37.118
"No, I always kept still when I was told," said Marilla, trying to speak sternly but warming to Davy's hugs.

57
00:05:37.119 --> 00:05:42.410
"Well, I suppose that was because you're a girl," said Davy.

58
00:05:42.411 --> 00:05:46.367
"Dora can sit still. But it's not as fun."

59
00:05:46.368 --> 00:05:54.814
"How can you be such a naughty boy when your poor mother's funeral was today?" demanded Marilla despairingly.

60
00:05:54.815 --> 00:05:58.836
"But she was glad to die," said Davy confidentially.

61
00:05:58.837 --> 00:06:04.857
"I know, because she told me so. Mother was tired of being sick.

62
00:06:04.858 --> 00:06:07.580
We had a long talk before she died.

63
00:06:07.581 --> 00:06:12.594
She said you would take me and Dora, and I would be a good boy."

64
00:06:12.595 --> 00:06:16.066
They arrived at Green Gables, and Anne greeted them.

65
00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:30.237
Dora calmly allowed herself to be kissed, but Davy gave Anne a hearty hug and cheerfully announced, "I'm Mr. Davy Keith."
